The Acts	Acts	51	10	1	And there was a certain man in Caesarea, named Cornelius, a centurion of that which is called the Italian band;
The Acts	Acts	51	10	2	A religious man, and fearing God with all his house, giving much alms to the people, and always praying to God.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	3	This man saw in a vision manifestly, about the ninth hour of the day, an angel of God coming in unto him, and saying to him: Cornelius.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	4	And he, beholding him, being seized with fear, said: What is it, Lord? And he said to him: Thy prayers and thy alms are ascended for a memorial in the sight of God.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	5	And now send men to Joppe, and call hither one Simon, who is surnamed Peter:
The Acts	Acts	51	10	6	He lodgeth with one Simon a tanner, whose house is by the sea side. He will tell thee what thou must do.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	7	And when the angel who spoke to him was departed, he called two of his household servants, and a soldier who feared the Lord, of them that were under him.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	8	To whom when he had related all, he sent them to Joppe.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	9	And on the next day, whilst they were going on their journey, and drawing nigh to the city, Peter went up to the higher parts of the house to pray, about the sixth hour.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	10	And being hungry, he was desirous to taste somewhat. And as they were preparing, there came upon him an ecstasy of mind.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	11	And he saw the heaven opened, and a certain vessel descending, as it were a great linen sheet let down by the four corners from heaven to the earth:
The Acts	Acts	51	10	12	Wherein were all manner of fourfooted beasts, and creeping things of the earth, and fowls of the air.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	13	And there came a voice to him: Arise, Peter; kill and eat.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	14	But Peter said: Far be it from me; for I never did eat any thing that is common and unclean.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	15	And the voice spoke to him again the second time: That which God hath cleansed, do not thou call common.
The Acts	Acts	51	10	16	And this was done thrice; and presently the vessel was taken up into heaven.
