The Acts	Acts	51	20	38	Being grieved most of all for the word which he had said, that they should see his face no more. And they brought him on his way to the ship.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	1	And when it came to pass that, being parted from them, we set sail, we came with a straight course to Coos, and the day following to Rhodes, and from thence to Patara.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	2	And when we had found a ship sailing over to Phenice, we went aboard, and set forth.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	3	And when we had discovered Cyprus, leaving it on the left hand, we sailed into Syria, and came to Tyre: for there the ship was to unlade her burden.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	4	And finding disciples, we tarried there seven days: who said to Paul through the Spirit, that he should not go up to Jerusalem.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	5	And the days being expired, departing we went forward, they all bringing us on our way, with their wives and children, till we were out of the city: and we kneeled down on the shore, and we prayed.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	6	And when we had bid one another farewell, we took ship; and they returned home.
