The Acts	Acts	51	21	15	And after those days, being prepared, we went up to Jerusalem.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	16	And there went also with us some of the disciples from Caesarea, bringing with them one Manson a Cyprian, an old disciple, with whom we should lodge.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	17	And when we were come to Jerusalem, the brethren received us gladly.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	18	And the day following, Paul went in with us unto James; and all the ancients were assembled.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	19	Whom when he had saluted, he related particularly what things God had wrought among the Gentiles by his ministry.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	20	But they hearing it, glorified God, and said to him: Thou seest, brother, how many thousands there are among the Jews that have believed: and they are all zealous for the law.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	21	Now they have heard of thee that thou teachest those Jews, who are among the Gentiles, to depart from Moses: saying, that they ought not to circumcise their children, nor walk according to the custom.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	22	What is it therefore? the multitude must needs come together: for they will hear that thou art come.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	23	Do therefore this that we say to thee. We have four men, who have a vow on them.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	24	Take these, and sanctify thyself with them: and bestow on them, that they may shave their heads: and all will know that the things which they have heard of thee, are false; but that thou thyself also walkest keeping the law.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	25	But as touching the Gentiles that believe, we have written, decreeing that they should only refrain themselves from that which has been offered to idols, and from blood, and from things strangled, and from fornication.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	26	Then Paul took the men, and the next day being purified with them, entered into the temple, giving notice of the accomplishment of the days of purification, until an oblation should be offered for every one of them.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	27	But when the seven days were drawing to an end, those Jews that were of Asia, when they saw him in the temple, stirred up all the people, and laid hands upon him, crying out:
The Acts	Acts	51	21	28	Men of Israel, help: This is the man that teacheth all men everywhere against the people, and the law, and this place; and moreover hath brought in Gentiles into the temple, and hath violated this holy place.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	29	(For they had seen Trophimus the Ephesian in the city with him, whom they supposed that Paul had brought into the temple.)
The Acts	Acts	51	21	30	And the whole city was in an uproar: and the people ran together. And taking Paul, they drew him out of the temple, and immediately the doors were shut.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	31	And as they went about to kill him, it was told the tribune of the band, That all Jerusalem was in confusion.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	32	Who, forthwith taking with him soldiers and centurions, ran down to them. And when they saw the tribune and the soldiers they left off beating Paul.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	33	Then the tribune coming near, took him, and commanded him to be bound with two chains: and demanded who he was, and what he had done.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	34	And some cried one thing, some another, among the multitude. And when he could not know the certainty for the tumult, he commanded him to be carried into the castle.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	35	And when he was come to the stairs, it fell out that he was carried by the soldiers, because of the violence of the people.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	36	For the multitude of the people followed after, crying: Away with him.
The Acts	Acts	51	21	37	And as Paul was about to be brought into the castle, he saith to the tribune: May I speak something to thee? Who said: Canst thou speak Greek?
The Acts	Acts	51	21	38	Art not thou that Egyptian who before these days didst raise a tumult, and didst lead forth into the desert four thousand men that were murderers?
The Acts	Acts	51	21	39	But Paul said to him: I am a Jew of Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no mean city. And I beseech thee, suffer me to speak to the people.
